From: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: HW GRO v5 refinements

Remaining deltas of the net-next v5 "add HW GRO offload support"
series vs what this tree already carries (916-02 + 920-xx rework +
975 NETIF_F_GRO_HW migration):

1. Validate the hardware-reported aggregate count against
   AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGG_COUNT before building the LRO skb, so a
   bogus msg2 can't produce garbage gso_segs/gso_size. Moved the
   read before any skb allocation to keep the error path leak-free.
2. Only patch the TCP timestamp echo reply (TSecr) into the header
   when the descriptor field is non-zero: the field is pre-zeroed in
   the posted descriptor, so non-zero means the hardware actually
   populated it. Previously a zero would clobber a valid TSecr.
3. Disable the FE LRO engine in ndo_stop when the device has
   NETIF_F_GRO_HW enabled, so stale FE LRO state can't outlive the
   netdev and spuriously -EBUSY a later open of another device
   sharing the QDMA.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -739,6 +739,10 @@ static struct sk_buff *airoha_qdma_lro_r
 	l2_len = FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_L2_LEN_MASK, msg2);
 	len = FIELD_GET(QDMA_DESC_LEN_MASK, desc_ctrl);
 
+	agg_count = FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_AGG_COUNT_MASK, msg2);
+	if (agg_count > AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGG_COUNT)
+		return NULL;
+
 	if (ipv4) {
 		struct iphdr *iph;
 
@@ -814,7 +818,15 @@ static struct sk_buff *airoha_qdma_lro_r
 			u8 *ptr = (u8 *)th + sizeof(*th) + 2 * sizeof(__be32);
 			__le32 tcp_ts_reply = READ_ONCE(desc->tcp_ts_reply);
 
-			put_unaligned_be32(le32_to_cpu(tcp_ts_reply), ptr);
+			/* The field is pre-zeroed in the posted descriptor,
+			 * so a non-zero value is the hardware confirming the
+			 * timestamp echo reply is valid. Leave TSecr
+			 * untouched otherwise, since the hardware may not
+			 * populate it for every aggregate.
+			 */
+			if (tcp_ts_reply)
+				put_unaligned_be32(le32_to_cpu(tcp_ts_reply),
+						   ptr);
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -845,7 +857,6 @@ static struct sk_buff *airoha_qdma_lro_r
 			q->buf_size);
 
 	shinfo->gso_type = ipv4 ? SKB_GSO_TCPV4 : SKB_GSO_TCPV6;
-	agg_count = FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_AGG_COUNT_MASK, msg2);
 	shinfo->gso_size = DIV_ROUND_UP(data_len, agg_count);
 	shinfo->gso_segs = agg_count;
 
@@ -2213,6 +2224,10 @@ static int airoha_dev_stop(struct net_de
 		airoha_set_gdm_port_fwd_cfg(qdma->eth,
 					    REG_GDM_FWD_CFG(port->id),
 					    FE_PSE_PORT_DROP);
+
+	if (netdev->features & NETIF_F_GRO_HW)
+		airoha_fe_lro_disable(qdma->eth, qdma - &dev->eth->qdma[0]);
+
 	airoha_qdma_stop(qdma);
 	airoha_update_netdev_features(dev);
 
